    "turn_text": "So I really had, and my first child was born. And then 96, then Congressman Durban ran for Paul Simon Senate seat. I got asked to look at it again, which is much better than saying I'd like to look at it again because then you engender more support. Had a five member primary. I won that by, I think, over 50% of the vote. And then a very, very, one of the closest races in the nation in 96 against now return state Rep. J Hoffman. Yes. Conservative Democrat on kind of social and guns issues that's big in Southern Illinois and only 1200 votes. So it was declared victory at 3 a.m. in the morning and held the seat ever since.",
