    "turn_idx": 68,
    "turn_text": "that's just the way the Founding Fathers designed it. So to follow on the U.S. commitments to the NATO, the North Atlantic Council and NATO itself, we have like a shadow organization called the NATO Parliamentary Assembly where members from legislative branches from all the NATO countries and the aspirants meet regularly, officially three times a year and then in subcommittees other times, mostly in Europe because that's where most of the countries are, sometimes in Canada, sometimes we meet here in the United States to talk about policies of the North Atlantic Treaty Organization and to make sure that the legislative branches of our government's at least are giving some input to the North Atlantic Council.",
