    "turn_text": "this is a fun fact. From the day I was born to the day I graduated high school, Illinois had a Republican governor. from 1984 to 2002. And then 2002, our good friend Rob LeGoyevich won the governorship, and it's been a democratic governor domination ever since. In fact, in 2006, even though Rob LeGoyevich had a 30 percent or below approval rating, he still won the governorship by 10 percentage points. So that kind of signals how bad your party has done on this front in the last 12 to something years. But this year, there's a little bit more hope because Pat Quinn, Blagojevic's successor after Blagojevic went to jail in an Illinois tradition, of course. Also is very unpopular for various reasons. In fact, I saw a poll where he actually had sub-30 approval ratings, but I guess in typical Illinois Republican form, there's a pretty crowded primary.",
